From 7fb11f14d24906c619ac215cffd2ad627dbf5c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:16:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, win32u: Show a MetalFX game the main display divided
 by its upscale factor.

Mullion's MetalFX spatial scaler upscales each frame to the display, so a game should render at the
display's size divided by the factor. A game MetalSharp launched (its folder has .metalsharp/launch.env)
on the Mullion backend reads the factor Mullion uses for it from $MULLION_CONFIG_FILE and $MULLION_CONFIG
(d3d12.metalSpatialUpscale[Factor], or d3d11's). win32u then shows that process alone a primary display of
the nearest size of the display's exact aspect ratio, with the display's own mode as the physical one, so
Wine scales its windows to the screen as for an emulated mode change, and its mode changes are emulated.

The saved-resolution fit aims at that size too, a saved size of the whole display (or a larger one) is
replaced even without a record, and Remedy's Northlight (Control's renderer.ini) joins the known settings.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/saved_resolution.c | 286 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c            |  68 +++++++
 include/wine/unixlib.h             |   4 +
 3 files changed, 328 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

